From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tompta1 <546706+tompta1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:07:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Input: apple_z2: Add the K1 controller of the iPad Pro 2

The iPad Pro 12.9 (2017) and 10.5 (A10X; ADT multi-touch
"hid-transport,k1") boot their K1 touch controller with HBPP14 like the
other iPads, then report float contacts in gen2 interrupt packets read
with a counter. Add a K1 variant:

- power-up from the device tree: analog supply, LDO GPIO, the display sync
  pins in their function state, the reference clock, then 15 ms;
- the firmware SPI clock and chip-select delay from the firmware's
  configuration, long replies in short chunks with chip select held;
- after the upload, the surface report is read and the input device is
  registered with the controller's own extent;
- runtime interrupt packets are read with the counter, checked and their
  contacts reported through the J172 float parser, a whole frame dropped
  when it repeats a finger or carries a bad coordinate;
- a runtime transfer error stops touch until the next resume, which boots
  the controller again; the controller is given 100 ms to settle before
  DeviceInfo.

Matches for the four iPad Pro 2 boards. Nothing changes for the other
variants: the shared HBPP14 checks become one helper with the same
result, and the J172/J71b parser keeps skipping a single bad contact.

[Orchard: from OrchardLinux/orchard#205 (tompta1, 09038adf),
 kernel/patches/drivers/input/0033, 0034, 0035 squashed. The variant is
 named for the K1 controller instead of the J120 and matched for J121,
 J207 and J208 too; the whole-frame check applies to K1 only instead of
 also changing the J71b/J172 parser; the J120 bring-up logging and boot
 stage tracking dropped; the input device is named from the chip info.]

Assisted-by: LLM
